More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (221–230)
221. Insecure Direct Object Mapping
Insecure Direct Object Reference
Applications expose object identifiers that allow access to other users’ resources.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
222. Cloud Metadata Exposure
Cloud Metadata Exposure
Applications expose access to internal cloud metadata services containing credentials.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $10,000
223. Open S3 Bucket / Public Storage Exposure
Cloud Storage Misconfiguration
Sensitive files stored in publicly accessible cloud storage.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
224. Subdomain Enumeration Data Leak
Subdomain Enumeration Exposure
Sensitive services exposed through forgotten or hidden subdomains.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
225. Weak Encryption Implementation
Weak Encryption
Applications use outdated or insecure encryption algorithms.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
226. Hardcoded Credentials
Hardcoded Credentials
Usernames, passwords, or tokens embedded in source code or mobile apps.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
227. Exposed Environment Variables
Environment Variable Exposure
Sensitive configuration values like API keys exposed through environment files.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
228. Source Map Exposure
Source Map Exposure
JavaScript source maps reveal original application code and internal logic.
💰 Typical payout: $100 – $2,000
229. Improper Access Control in GraphQL
GraphQL Authorization Vulnerability
GraphQL resolvers fail to enforce proper access permissions.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
230. Mobile App Debuggable Build
Debuggable Mobile Application
Production mobile apps shipped with debugging enabled.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
